<title>BELGIUM: EU clears Polish TV venture.</title>
<headline>EU clears Polish TV venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Tuesday it had cleared the creation of a Polish television joint venture between European Media group CLT-UFA and the U.S. company Universal, a subsidiary of Seagram.</p>
<p>The Commission said that although the operation had a European dimension, as the parent companies meet the turnover thresholds set in the EU's merger rules, the alliance would have no impact on competition in the European market.</p>
<p>The joint venture, to be called RTL-7, will broadcast general entertainment programmes via cable and satellite in Polish.</p>
<p>CLT-UFA is controlled by Luxembourg holding company Audiofina and Bertelsmann of Germany. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
